<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 9.925 percent on Monday from 9.987 percent at the previous auction on March 3.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 751.450 million pounds, replace bills worth 739.550 million maturing on Tuesday . The treasury had asked for 700 million pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Sept 9, 1997 (Sept 2, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.925 percent (9.987)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 751.450 million (630.575 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,676.650 million (982.675 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.701-9.946 percent (9.516-10.028)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.701-10.101 percent (9.516-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 55 (130)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 177 (174)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>((-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1))</p>
</text>
